Label gpu_vram in GiB rather than as a ratio

sysmon reports ram both ways — ram_used in bytes and ram_pct — and disk four
ways, but VRAM only as gpu_vram, whose label is hardcoded to a percentage.
That leaves it the odd one out beside ram on the same bar.

The gauge fill and the gpu_vram_* thresholds read the normalized ratio from
normalizedFromStats, which this does not touch, so only the label changes —
giving gpu_vram the shape RamUsed already has.

--- a/src/shell/bar/widgets/sysmon_widget.cpp
+++ b/src/shell/bar/widgets/sysmon_widget.cpp
@@ -935,11 +935,8 @@
     return std::nullopt;

   case SysmonStat::GpuVram:
-    if (stats.gpuVramUsedBytes.has_value() && stats.gpuVramTotalBytes.has_value() && *stats.gpuVramTotalBytes > 0) {
-      return std::format(
-          "{:.0f}%",
-          100.0 * static_cast<double>(*stats.gpuVramUsedBytes) / static_cast<double>(*stats.gpuVramTotalBytes)
-      );
+    if (stats.gpuVramUsedBytes.has_value()) {
+      return FormatUnits::formatBinaryBytesAsGib(*stats.gpuVramUsedBytes);
     }
     return std::nullopt;

